      "evidence_type": "published tag insertion at this exact site",
      "functional_impact_measured": "Construct used for stable lentiviral expression and co-immunoprecipitation experiments; surface display confirmed by experimental use, but no explicit transferrin-binding or endocytosis assay reported for the tagged protein alone.",
      "confidence": "high",
      "rationale": "L2 explicitly states the HA tag was inserted between amino acids 111 and 112 of TfR1. Python confirms seq[110]='E' (residue 111) and seq[111]='P' (residue 112), both within the extracellular span (87\u2013760), 25 residues from the TM boundary \u2014 well clear of the \u22653 aa minimum. The construct is full-length and membrane-anchored, not a soluble ectodomain. L1 describes the same construct but names no residue; L2 is the grounding clip. Full-length human TfR1 expressed from a lentiviral vector (pLenti_HA-human-TfR1) in stably transduced mammalian cells; HA tag inserted between residues 111 and 112, placing it in the extracellular ectodomain 25 aa from the TM boundary (TM ends at residue 86).",
